{
  "name": "Nightly check that every post ID is officialized",
  "today": "Each night the gas book administrators must officialize every post ID (book) so the V@R and credit systems pick it up. Since October 2000, after a missed West-NW-GDL book put the desk on Risk's daily list of non-officialized books (sent to Sally Beck and reviewed weekly by Rick Buy), one person per desk group runs an Excel macro by hand: they enter the date and the Portfolio and Book codes, and the macro lists the books that are officialized. The groups led by Gossett, Baumbach, Kelly, Giron and Keiser each got this file, and staff pass round changed versions of it. Regional controllers also get an end-of-night sheet confirming all books are officialized, and Risk keeps its own daily list of misses. No system holds the full list of books each admin must officialize, so Darron Giron writes it out by hand when another group asks (Rahmaan in July, Connie Sutton and Susan Trevino in November 2000). The check used before the macro compared positions only, so it missed post IDs with no net position. Credit needs those flat books officialized too.",
  "change": "Keep one list of the post IDs each book admin must officialize, and have the risk system email any that are not officialized by cut-off, replacing the hand-run nightly macros.",
  "explanation": "Risk and IT set up one list (registry) of the post IDs each book admin must officialize each night. The lists Darron already writes out by hand are the starting point. At a set time before cut-off each night, the risk system compares that list with the books marked official and emails each owner any of their post IDs still not officialized, flat books included. The same report becomes the controllers' end-of-night sheet and Risk's daily tracking list. Desks stop running the Excel macro by hand and stop maintaining their own copies of it. Book admins only act when they get an exception email. When another group asks which books are officialized, the answer comes from the registry.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/533.eml",
      "quote": "I think Jason has been running the official post id macro most nights, but we need to have the last person finished do it every day."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/582.eml",
      "quote": "The macro in this file will query all official books for given Portfolio and Book codes.  Use it to make sure all your postid's that need to be, are officialized each night."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/595.eml",
      "quote": "We have been tracking books that are not officialized on a daily basis."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/500.eml",
      "quote": "I have updated the list to include every book we officialize each night."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/492.eml",
      "quote": "I believe this is all of the Enovate/EMW books that are officialized each night."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/582.eml",
      "quote": "To run this file all that has to be done is enter the date and have the Portfolio and Book CD entered in also.",
      "note": "The macro is run by hand each night, with the codes typed in. Dutch Quigley sent it to five desk-group leads (Gossett, Baumbach, Kelly, Giron, Keiser), so roughly five runs a night."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/533.eml",
      "quote": "All regional controllers will receive a sheet at the end of the night, verifying that all books are officialized.",
      "note": "A separate nightly verification sheet goes to every regional controller. The automatic report would replace it."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/595.eml",
      "quote": "If a postid has a net position and is not officialized, it will be caught using this procedure.  It will not, however, if the postid does not have a position.",
      "note": "The earlier position-based check missed flat post IDs. A registry-based check catches them whatever their position."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/580.eml",
      "quote": "This one requires a comment in all post-id's to pull in only those.",
      "note": "Staff keep changing and passing round their own versions of the macro file. A central check removes this upkeep."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/401.eml",
      "quote": "Credit picks up all officalized books.  If a book is not officialized, it picks up the previous day's position.",
      "note": "A missed book, flat ones included, gives credit wrong data. This is why the nightly check matters."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/590.eml",
      "quote": "We are currently looking into a query which will allow us to see all of our officialized books each night.",
      "note": "The desk itself wanted a system view of the officialized books."
    }
  ],
  "stalls": [],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": null,
  "minutes": 30
}

