  "change": "Re-book ENA deals 290657 and 290652 once to match Enron Canada's booking so the monthly ~$434 OA difference stops.",
  "reason": "This is a one-off fix to a single wrongly booked deal that the person doing the work had already asked for, not a change to how the work is done, and its savings depend on a deal term the mail never gives.",
  "research": "Only a pattern would change this: several deals in the mail where ENA and Enron Canada book the same intercompany trade differently and settlements has to chase the desk each month, which would support a process change such as a booking check between the two entities."
}

{
